<%# Destructive action (delete, cancel, remove photos): a button_to that asks the
    browser to confirm first (Turbo's data-turbo-confirm), drawn in the problem red.
    Gating stays with the caller: wrap HARD deletes in
    current_user.can_delete? so limited admins never see them.
    Locals:
      label   (String, required) e.g. "Delete"
      url     (String, required) the action's path
      confirm (String, required) the question, e.g. "Permanently delete this review?"
      method  (Symbol, optional, default :delete) :post for actions like cancel
      variant (Symbol, optional, default :link) :link for table rows,
              :button for page headers and panel footers
      params  (Hash, optional) extra params sent with the form
    Example:
      render "admin/shared/confirm_button", label: "Delete", url: admin_presentation_path(deck),
             confirm: "Are you sure you want to delete this presentation?" %>
<% variant = local_assigns.fetch(:variant, :link).to_sym %>
<% classes = if variant == :button
     "inline-flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-2xl border border-rsvp-no/30 bg-white px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-rsvp-no transition hover:bg-rsvp-no/10 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-rsvp-no/40"
   else
     "cursor-pointer text-sm font-semibold text-rsvp-no underline-offset-4 hover:underline focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-rsvp-no/40 rounded"
   end %>
<%= button_to label, url,
      method: local_assigns.fetch(:method, :delete),
      params: local_assigns.fetch(:params, {}),
      class: classes,
      form: { class: "inline", data: { turbo_confirm: confirm } } %>
